# The ACCEPTING side's mirror: a genuinely non-regular RBox.
# r o s subseteq s together with s o r subseteq r has no strict linear order on roles
# making both chains regular, so the RBox is inadmissible.
# Expect: a COLLECTIVE RBox failure -- the ENTIRE RBox goes to coverage.omitted and
# the run is inconclusive, with the witness reported as a diagnostic. HOWL does not
# delete a witness and classify the projected RBox: a witness is not a removal set,
# and the choice among alternative deletions is not canonical.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty .
:s owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :r :s ) .
:r owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :s :r ) .
